From 941ddaac0c84daba498e93b7f7f058011b71a753 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:11:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 247/250] parse: a method-call turbofish may start with `<-`
 (a negative const argument)

time 0.3.54 (ani-cli-rs 0.11.0) and 0.3.55 (cargo-c 0.10.25),
formatting/formattable.rs:127:

    error:0: Unexpected token TOK_THINARROW_LEFT, expected TOK_LT
    formattable.rs:450:1: note: From here

`year.narrow::<-99, 99>()`: the lexer makes one `<-` token out of the `<`
and the negative literal const generic argument that follows it.
Parse_Path already splits it back into `<` `-` for path generics
(`ri16::<-9_999, 9_999>::new_unchecked`, line 123) and type generics
(`ri8<-25, 25>`, utc_offset.rs:32); the method-call arm of the postfix
expression parser only knew how to split `<<`. It now puts a `-` back the
same way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/src/parse/expr.cpp b/src/parse/expr.cpp
index e4c9248f..c6ac8c40 100644
--- a/src/parse/expr.cpp
+++ b/src/parse/expr.cpp
@@ -1190,6 +1190,11 @@ ExprNodeP Parse_ExprFC(TokenStream& lex)
                     if( lex.getTokenIf(TOK_DOUBLE_LT) ) {
                         lex.putback(Token(TOK_LT));
                     }
+                    else if( lex.getTokenIf(TOK_THINARROW_LEFT) ) {
+                        // A negative literal const argument lexes as `<-` (`year.narrow::<-99, 99>()`, time 0.3.54
+                        // formattable.rs:127); paths and types already split it (Parse_Path)
+                        lex.putback(Token(TOK_DASH));
+                    }
                     else {
                         GET_CHECK_TOK(tok, lex, TOK_LT);
                     }
